SECTION 1+2 -- THE RE-REGISTERED RULE (pre-committed today, binding December):
  LEVEL 1 (the RIDGE GATE -- the falsifier's kill): ridge ABSENT (sexc outside [1.15,1.22]
    or sigma < 10 or break/rise/level fail) -> DISFAVORED = KILL, regardless of n_pass.
  LEVEL 2 (at ridge CONFIRMED): 9/9 = CONFIRMED-STRONG (DECLARED UNREACHABLE at December N,
    P = 0.000; the 20-sigma gate stays registered as the STRONG condition);
    7-8 = CONFIRMED-WEAK (ridge > 10 sigma + verticals MIXED: the EFE-cap + ridge physics at
    the envelope level, the verticals pending better astrometry);
    <= 6 = SPLIT (ridge confirmed, verticals systematically anti-correlated or collapsed: a
    genuine tension -- NOT a kill; the identification's zero-parameter statement stands).
  The December pre-commitment threshold table (frozen; every test bar unchanged from G165/G112):
    verdict         n_pass   ridge condition                 verticals' sign consistency
    CONFIRMED-STRONG  9/9   R-RIDGE30.7 >= 20 sigma, sexc in [1.15,1.22]   all 5 pass, signs as registered
    CONFIRMED-WEAK    7-8   R-LEVEL+R-BREAK7.4+R-NOTFLAT pass AND ridge-sigma > 10
                                                               mixed: <=1 of 5 fails, no F1/F2/F3 kill
    SPLIT             <=6   ridge confirmed (as WEAK)          >= 2 of 5 fail on the anti-sign side
                                                               (or any F1/F2/F3 kill) -- genuine tension
    DISFAVORED        any   ridge ABSENT (sexc<1.15 / sigma<10 / no break / flat) = KILL, no rescue
  RE-READ: at December N the mechanical n_pass <= 4 tail (P ~ 0.07-0.09, G225) is the vertical
    sector collapsing at the FROZEN precision (the bars sit ~1 sigma from the forecast central
    values, G225 V3) WITH the ridge confirmed -- re-read as SPLIT, not DISFAVORED.  The kill
    is reserved for the ridge absent.  This is the pre-registered honesty floor, not a re-tuning.
