VERDICTS
  V1 [the re-registered rule]: the DR4 falsifier is re-armed at the reachable verdict class.
     The kill = the ridge ABSENT (no rise, no 7.4-kAU break, sexc < 1.15, or sigma < 10) ->
     DISFAVORED, no rescue (FALSIFIER_MATRIX row 1 stands).  At ridge confirmed: 7-8/9 = WEAK
     (verticals mixed), <= 6/9 = SPLIT (verticals anti-correlated/collapsed = genuine tension,
     NOT a kill).  9/9 = STRONG declared UNREACHABLE in December (P = 0.000 at N <= 5,000;
     the 20-sigma R-RIDGE30.7 gate needs N_usable ~ 5760).  Every test bar is unchanged
     (G165/G112 frozen); only the verdict READING is re-stated, before the data.
  V2 [the December expectations at the re-registered class] (G225 primary cells, re-read):
     N=2000, 30 uas:  P(WEAK)=0.506 P(SPLIT)=0.494 P(DISFAVORED)=0.000 P(STRONG)=0.000
     N=5000, 30 uas:  P(WEAK)=0.474 P(SPLIT)=0.526 P(DISFAVORED)=0.000 P(STRONG)=0.000
     the ridge registers 11.5 sigma (N=2000) / 18.4 sigma (N=5000) in EVERY realization -- the ridge is the
     number to watch, and it is confirmed in 100% of realizations at every documented N.
     At the extrapolated best case N=6288: see the cells above (P(STRONG) turns on).
  V3 [the honest statement]: the DR4 falsifier, re-armed at the reachable precision.  The
     theory's own forecast (the mocks ARE the registered prediction) lands MODAL CONFIRMED-
     WEAK ~ SPLIT with the ridge confirmed at 11.5-18.4 sigma in every realization;
     P(CONFIRMED-STRONG) = 0.000 and P(DISFAVORED) = 0.000 at the re-registered class (the
     kill requires the ridge absent, which the forecast never produces).  The December number
     to watch is the ridge sigma and the 5 verticals' sign consistency -- WEAK vs SPLIT --
     not P(STRONG).  The N ~ 5,760 gate is at the top of the honest extrapolation from the
     DR4 documentation (x2.8 PM precision over WB-33's 10,624/802 DR3 catalog): a best-case
     N ~ 6288 makes the STRONG outcome reachable, but it is NOT the December base case.
